      "content": "thanks, but it still feels like you're trying to play it safe. you keep saying \"holistic\" and \"nuanced,\" but in a real debate, people want a clear direction. if we go with your suggestion of centering systemic injustices to \"prepare them for the real world,\" aren't we basically admitting that the traditional \"triumphs\" approach is outdated and insufficient for raising responsible citizens? it seems like you're saying one is just a \"simplified\" version and the other is the \"truthful\" one. isn't that a bit of a biased take?",
